 34P  c  2009Be26: 20, 24, 25, 30, and 44-MeV {+18}O beams were used. The target
 34P 2c  was 200-|mg/cm{+2} 97%-enriched {+18}O on a 12.7-|mm Ta backing.       
 34P 3c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, p|g-coin, and |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, 
 34P 4c  |p, multipolarities, and lifetimes using DSAM lineshape analysis.      
 34P 5c  Comparisons to shell model calculations.                               
 34P  c  At FSU E({+18}O)=24 and 44 MeV. |g rays were detected by the           
 34P 2c  Compton-suppressed high-purity germanium (HPGe) array, consisting of 6 
 34P 3c  single crystal HPGe detectors and 3 four-crystal clover detectors. Each
 34P 4c  Ge detector was surrounded by bismuth germinate (BGO) crystals used for
 34P 5c  Compton suppression. Charged particles were detected by a segmented    
 34P 6c  |DE-E Si telescope.                                                    
 34P  c  At LBNL E({+18}O)=20, 25, and 30 MeV. Charged particles were detected  
 34P 2c  by the Silicon Telescope Array for Reaction Studies (STARS), consisting
 34P 3c  of a |DE-E Si detector telescope. |g rays were detected by the         
 34P 4c  Livermore Berkeley Array for Collaborative Experiments (LiBerACE)      
 34P 5c  consisting of five HPGe clover detectors.                              
